{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Every word of Elohim is refined</b> — as in: \"The words of YHWH are pure words,\" and they are the commandments, refined like refined gold, and in them is the wisdom of fear of HaShem, and it is not fitting to engage in anything other than them. Therefore, \"do not add to His words,\" you Ithiel, as in \"you shall not add to it and you shall not subtract from it.\"" "<b>A shield</b> — the mem is added, and likewise מנגן, like משברי אל." "<b>Eloah, El — two</b> — [ה-ז] three joined, in the manner of prayer."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {2 "The bracketed [ה-ז] appears to be a textual notation, possibly indicating letters or a variant marking; its referent is uncertain so it is rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:30.749387241Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}